        "id": 1079148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-06T00:10:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose we can check for EMFILE, and return INT_MAX or something, but it seems unlikely that we\u0027ll actually be able to get through to the point where we can dump before something else notices and explodes (and I don\u0027t think we actually handle being *actually* out of fds in the fdtrack dumping code either: we don\u0027t do the \"clone a thread with a separate fd table and close a bunch of random fds to clear up space\" trick).\n\nThe thresholds are set to be way lower than the actual maximum, so hopefully we\u0027ll have dumped before then?",
      "parentUuid": "c1aeaf5d_9a9b5845",
      "revId": "319e627a1f79d19a6b42471199ca5ebde6f09d33",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
